            {
                "entry_id": "1a2112e7-c8f7-3b62-a174-14bf7fd677eb",
                "word": "manumission",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "df40c61c-7649-479b-89a1-7b4832e2dfd6",
                        "entry_id": "1a2112e7-c8f7-3b62-a174-14bf7fd677eb",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "manumissions"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "350367f7-7234-3cd6-ad8e-47e73f51f55c",
                        "entry_id": "1a2112e7-c8f7-3b62-a174-14bf7fd677eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Action d’affranchir un esclave ou un serf."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ancient"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "30c274db-2987-4840-ae9b-e56b776dbc5d",
                                "sense_id": "350367f7-7234-3cd6-ad8e-47e73f51f55c",
                                "text": "…car les raisons que j’ai données plus haut ne sont pas les seules qui s’opposaient à cette espèce de manumission."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44c5a430-8854-4b75-a702-39235f2ea4e3",
                                "sense_id": "350367f7-7234-3cd6-ad8e-47e73f51f55c",
                                "text": "L'action fut l'argent de manumission de la machinerie, et, en son essence, l'actionnaire représente et représentera constamment le propriétaire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c405003d-9212-496a-8eb2-8128e5eb274c",
                        "source_entry_id": "1a2112e7-c8f7-3b62-a174-14bf7fd677eb",
                        "source_sense_id": "350367f7-7234-3cd6-ad8e-47e73f51f55c",
                        "target_lang_word": "manumission",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "manumission",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e5f0d7d-80fd-3794-a584-68ddd6ab1573",
                                        "entry_id": "7504ec65-7c9d-30b5-b917-90ca64f4c0b8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Release from slavery or other legally sanctioned servitude; the giving of freedom; the act of manumitting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5411d131-d13c-4750-89af-7a196bf5f8b3",
                                                "sense_id": "5e5f0d7d-80fd-3794-a584-68ddd6ab1573",
                                                "text": "The manumission of the slaves in New York has been gradual."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2428979a-daaf-4711-ac9f-85ab3f2cbf59",
                                                "sense_id": "5e5f0d7d-80fd-3794-a584-68ddd6ab1573",
                                                "text": "The most important law of Augustus, was the lex oelia sentia, deserving of all praise, which related to the manumission of slaves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d14b0d10-18d1-477a-84c6-73bcebb602b1",
                                                "sense_id": "5e5f0d7d-80fd-3794-a584-68ddd6ab1573",
                                                "text": "In the west, and especially in Cornwall, the names of the serfs were mainly Celtic,—Griffith, Modred, Riol, and so forth,—as may be seen from the list of manumissions preserved in a mass-book at St. Petroc's, or Padstow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bd65825-572e-4859-a4cf-b3b4b62ad006",
                                                "sense_id": "5e5f0d7d-80fd-3794-a584-68ddd6ab1573",
                                                "text": "The more innocent dreamed of a manumission kindly bestowed by the new Emperor as one of a number of acts of justice and clemency proper to a new reign."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "550357dd-b72e-48b2-bfc5-362bd087feea",
                                                "sense_id": "5e5f0d7d-80fd-3794-a584-68ddd6ab1573",
                                                "text": "Rather than encouraging his countrymen to liberate their slaves, he opposed both private manumission and public emancipation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
